+**1. [Rule 3 - Blocking] Worktree #3099 path-resolution bug recovered**
+
+- **Found during:** Task 1 first Edit attempt.
+- **Issue:** Initial Edit tool calls used absolute paths (`/Users/adamthompson/CodeProjects/eha_care/.github/workflows/monorepo-deploy.yml`). Despite the worktree's CWD being correct, the Edit tool resolved those absolute paths to the **main repo** path (same prefix, no `.claude/worktrees/...` suffix in the absolute string). Both edits landed silently on the main repo at `/Users/adamthompson/CodeProjects/eha_care/.github/workflows/monorepo-deploy.yml` instead of the worktree.
+- **Detection:** Post-edit `grep -c 'BETTER_NPM_TOKEN='` against the worktree still returned 4 (unchanged from baseline). `cd /Users/adamthompson/CodeProjects/eha_care && git status` confirmed the main repo had unstaged modifications.
+- **Fix:**
+  1. `cd /Users/adamthompson/CodeProjects/eha_care && git checkout -- .github/workflows/monorepo-deploy.yml` — restored the main repo file to its HEAD state (no changes leaked to the main repo working tree).
+  2. Switched ALL subsequent Edit calls to use **relative paths** (`.github/workflows/monorepo-deploy.yml`). Per `references/worktree-path-safety.md`, relative paths inside a worktree always resolve against the worktree CWD, never against the main repo.
+- **Verification of fix:** Subsequent Edit calls landed on the worktree as confirmed by `sed -n` against the worktree file (BETTER_NPM_TOKEN gone from line 396, secrets: block present after build-args). Main repo `git status` returned empty (no leftover side-effects).
+- **Files affected:** None permanently — main repo restored before the unintended edits could be committed; worktree edits then applied cleanly.
+
+**2. [Rule 3 - Blocking] commitlint unavailable in worktree**
+
+- **Found during:** Task 1 first `git commit` attempt.
+- **Issue:** Pre-commit hook tried to invoke `commitlint` via `pnpm --filter <root> exec commitlint`. The worktree has no `node_modules` installed (worktrees are bare checkouts; `pnpm install` was never run). Hook exits with `ERR_PNPM_RECURSIVE_EXEC_FIRST_FAIL Command "commitlint" not found`.
+- **Fix:** Manually validated both task commit messages against `commitlint.config.ts` (located at `/Users/adamthompson/CodeProjects/eha_care/commitlint.config.ts` — extends `@commitlint/config-conventional`, scope-case allows lower/upper/camel/kebab/pascal, subject-case bans start/pascal/upper). Both header lengths confirmed ≤ 100 chars (Task 1 = 84, Task 2 = 82). Both use `fix(21-07): <lowercase subject>` shape. Then committed with `SKIP_HOOKS=1` per the parallel-execution worktree directive in the spawn prompt.
+- **Files affected:** N/A — commit messages are valid; only the hook invocation was bypassed.
